BUG: This commit reveals argument passing bugs when using int32 with 10+ arguments.

Test failures:
- RegisterFunc/Callback 10args: expected 55, got 45
- RegisterFunc/Callback 14args: expected 105, got 71
- RegisterFunc/CFunc 14args: expected 105, got 109 (wrong value!)
- SyscallN/CFunc 10args: expected 55, got 45
- SyscallN/CFunc 14args: expected 105, got 78
- RoundTrip/10args: expected 55, got garbage

This suggests purego has issues with stack packing or register assignment for 32-bit values when there are many arguments. The validation in these benchmarks caught real bugs that were hidden when using uintptr (which matches the native word size).
